---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, DATA_PATHS, AGENT_API, href } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'October 12, 2026';
const toc = [
  ['summary', 'Summary'],
  ['what-reelay-is', 'What Reelay is'],
  ['on-your-device', 'Data on your computer'],
  ['google-limited-use', 'Google and YouTube'],
  ['meta-compliance', 'Instagram, Facebook and Threads'],
  ['tiktok', 'TikTok'],
  ['bluesky', 'Bluesky'],
  ['sign-in-server', 'Reelay’s sign-in server'],
  ['other-connections', 'Other connections'],
  ['agents-and-ai', 'Agents and writing help'],
  ['we-collect', 'What we collect'],
  ['your-choices', 'Your choices and deletion'],
  ['children', 'Children'],
  ['changes', 'Changes'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy: ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="How Reelay handles your data: a desktop app that keeps your library, database and sign-ins on your computer, with full Google API Limited Use and Meta disclosures."
>
  <header class="doc-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Reelay is a desktop app. <strong>Your videos, your drafts and your sign-ins stay on your computer.</strong> This policy explains exactly what Reelay touches, where it keeps it, and who else ever sees it.</p>
      <p class="doc-meta">Last updated {lastUpdated} · Applies to Reelay Studio {SITE.version} and this website</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap doc-layout">
    <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <div>
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ol>{toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}</ol>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <div class="legal-content">
      <section id="summary" class="doc-summary">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We don’t run a cloud database. Your library, tickets, copy, transcripts and history live in a database file on your computer.</li>
          <li>Sign-in tokens are kept in the macOS Keychain or Windows Credential Manager, never in a file.</li>
          <li>Uploads and posts go straight from your computer to the platform. Your videos are never copied to a Reelay server.</li>
          <li>For TikTok, Instagram, Threads and Facebook sign-in, Reelay’s sign-in server swaps the sign-in code for tokens and forgets them within minutes. Google sign-in never touches it.</li>
          <li>The app has no analytics, no tracking and no advertising. We don’t sell data or use it to train AI models.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="what-reelay-is">
        <h2>1. What Reelay is</h2>
        <p>Reelay Studio (“Reelay”, “we”, “us”) is a desktop application for macOS and Windows. It helps creators bring in short-form videos they own or manage from TikTok, Instagram and YouTube, write copy for each platform they post to, check whether each video is ready, and publish it: automatically to YouTube, and to Bluesky, Threads and Facebook when the creator turns that on; by hand, with Reelay’s help, everywhere else.</p>
        <p>This policy covers the desktop app, the Reelay sign-in server described in <a href="#sign-in-server">section 7</a>, and this website.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="on-your-device">
        <h2>2. Data on your computer</h2>
        <p>Everything Reelay works with is stored on the computer it runs on, in places only your user account can read:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Your videos</strong> are saved in the library folder you choose (by default <code>~/Movies/Reelay</code> on a Mac and <code>Videos\Reelay</code> on Windows), with a manifest and a metadata file per video.</li>
          <li><strong>The database</strong>, <code>{DATA_PATHS.dbName}</code>, holds your profiles, tickets, platform copy, transcripts, provenance, publishing history, change history, automation rules and the search index. It lives in <code>{DATA_PATHS.mac}</code> on a Mac and <code>{DATA_PATHS.windows}</code> on Windows, a folder Reelay restricts to your user account.</li>
          <li><strong>Sign-in tokens and keys</strong> (YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, Threads and Facebook tokens, Bluesky App Passwords and the agent API key) are stored in the macOS Keychain or Windows Credential Manager, protected by your system login.</li>
          <li><strong>Logs</strong> are written to <code>~/Library/Logs/Reelay</code> on a Mac and <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Reelay\logs</code> on Windows. Secrets and tokens are never logged.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you choose to move the database into a folder synced by Google Drive, Dropbox, iCloud Drive or OneDrive so a teammate can open it, that provider stores the file under your account and its own privacy terms.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="google-limited-use">
        <h2>3. Google and YouTube</h2>
        <p>Reelay uses the YouTube Data API v3 so you can list your channel’s videos, upload videos you choose, and schedule them. You connect a channel under <strong>Accounts</strong> with Google sign-in.</p>

        <h3>3.1 Scopes Reelay requests</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.upload</code>: to upload the video files you choose to your channel, with the title, description, tags, visibility and publish time you set.</li>
          <li><code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly</code>: to list your channel and its uploads (including private and scheduled ones) so you can bring them into Reelay, and to confirm when a scheduled video has gone live.</li>
          <li><code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/yt-analytics.readonly</code>: requested only by Reelay’s own one-click Google sign-in, read-only, to show a video’s performance on its ticket. If you connect with your own Google Cloud project instead, this scope isn’t requested.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3.2 Limited Use</h3>
        <blockquote><p>Reelay’s use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p></blockquote>
        <p>In particular:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Google user data is used only to provide the features you use in Reelay, shown to you in the app.</li>
          <li>It is stored on your computer: tokens in your keychain, channel and video details in your local database. It is never sent to, or stored on, a Reelay server.</li>
          <li>It is not sold, not used for advertising, not used to determine creditworthiness, and not used to develop, improve or train generalized AI or machine-learning models.</li>
          <li>No person at Reelay can read it. It never leaves your computer except in the requests Reelay makes to Google on your behalf.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3.3 How Google sign-in works</h3>
        <p>Reelay uses the OAuth 2.0 flow for native apps described in RFC 8252. Your browser opens Google’s own sign-in page; Google sends the result back to a one-time loopback address on your computer (<code>http://127.0.0.1</code>, on a port chosen for that sign-in), protected with PKCE. Reelay never sees your Google password, and the exchange of the sign-in code for tokens happens on your computer, not on any Reelay server.</p>

        <h3>3.4 Revoking access</h3>
        <p>Click <strong>Disconnect</strong> on the channel under <strong>Accounts</strong>. Reelay asks Google to revoke the token at <code>https://oauth2.googleapis.com/revoke</code>, deletes it from your keychain, and removes the account from Reelay’s database. You can also remove Reelay at any time from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Account permissions</a>.</p>
        <p>Reviewers: see the <a href={`${href('/support')}#demo-verification`}>App Review notes</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="meta-compliance">
        <h2>4. Instagram, Facebook and Threads</h2>
        <p>Reelay can download videos from an Instagram profile, and publish to Facebook Pages and Threads when you turn automatic posting on for them. Instagram posting is done by you, in Instagram, with Prepare to Publish.</p>
        <p>When you sign in with Meta through Reelay’s own app, Reelay requests:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Instagram:</strong> <code>instagram_business_basic</code>, <code>instagram_business_content_publish</code>, and read-only <code>instagram_business_manage_insights</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Threads:</strong> <code>threads_basic</code>, <code>threads_content_publish</code>, and read-only <code>threads_manage_insights</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Facebook Pages:</strong> <code>pages_show_list</code>, <code>pages_manage_posts</code>, <code>pages_read_engagement</code>, and read-only <code>read_insights</code>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Tokens are stored in your keychain. Posts are sent from your computer directly to Meta’s APIs (<code>graph.facebook.com</code> and <code>graph.threads.com</code>). Threads fetches a video from a public link rather than accepting an upload, so for Threads Reelay serves the file from your own computer through a public address you set up (such as a Cloudflare Tunnel), on a link that expires after an hour.</p>
        <p>Meta sign-in passes through Reelay’s sign-in server (see <a href="#sign-in-server">section 7</a>). How to remove all Meta data is set out in our <a href={href('/data-deletion')}>User Data Deletion Instructions</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="tiktok">
        <h2>5. TikTok</h2>
        <p>Reelay downloads videos from TikTok profiles you own or manage, and reads the products tagged on a TikTok Shop video from its public page. Reelay does not post to TikTok: you post in TikTok’s own uploader, with Prepare to Publish.</p>
        <p>If you sign in with TikTok through Reelay’s app, Reelay requests <code>user.info.basic</code>, <code>video.list</code> and read-only <code>user.info.stats</code>. TikTok sign-in, token refresh and revocation pass through Reelay’s sign-in server, because TikTok requires the app secret for them.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="bluesky">
        <h2>6. Bluesky</h2>
        <p>Bluesky is connected with an App Password you create in Bluesky, stored in your keychain. When automatic posting is on, posts go from your computer directly to your Bluesky server.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sign-in-server">
        <h2>7. Reelay’s sign-in server</h2>
        <p>TikTok and Meta require an app secret to turn a sign-in code into tokens, and a secret shipped inside a desktop app can be extracted. So for those platforms only, Reelay runs a small sign-in server (<code>auth.reelay.app</code>) that holds Reelay’s app secrets and does that one step:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>It receives the sign-in code, exchanges it with the platform, and hands the tokens back to the app on your computer. A sign-in that isn’t collected is forgotten after 10 minutes.</li>
          <li>It also refreshes tokens when the app asks, and revokes TikTok tokens when you disconnect.</li>
          <li>It stores nothing after that. Secrets and tokens are never logged. It never receives your videos, your copy or your database.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Google sign-in, and signing in with your own developer keys or a Bluesky App Password, never involve this server.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="other-connections">
        <h2>8. Other connections the app makes</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Downloading</strong> fetches videos and their details from the platform you list them from.</li>
          <li><strong>Use browser sign-in</strong>, if you turn it on, lets Reelay read that browser’s sign-in cookies for the platform, on your computer, so it can download videos only visible to you. They are sent only to that platform.</li>
          <li><strong>Get SEO Suggestions</strong> sends your search terms to YouTube’s public search suggestions.</li>
          <li><strong>Import Sheet</strong> downloads a Google Sheet you share with a link.</li>
          <li><strong>LanguageTool</strong>, if installed, downloads its checker on first use and then runs offline.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Reelay has no analytics, crash reporting or update checks that send anything to us.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="agents-and-ai">
        <h2>9. Agents and writing help</h2>
        <p>Reelay’s Agent API listens on <code>{AGENT_API.host}:{AGENT_API.port}</code> on your computer and requires an access key from your keychain. If you connect an AI agent to it, what that agent sends to its own provider is governed by your agreement with that provider. Anything an agent asks to post, archive or change in bulk waits for a person’s approval.</p>
        <p>Writing help runs with a model on your own computer (Ollama or llama.cpp). Reelay does not send your captions to a paid AI service.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="we-collect">
        <h2>10. What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>From the app:</strong> nothing. We have no access to your computer, your library or your database.</li>
          <li><strong>From the sign-in server:</strong> only what is described in <a href="#sign-in-server">section 7</a>, for the minutes a sign-in takes.</li>
          <li><strong>From this website:</strong> standard web server logs (IP address, browser, pages requested) kept by our hosting provider for security. The site uses no advertising cookies or trackers.</li>
          <li><strong>When you email us:</strong> your address and message, used only to reply.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="your-choices">
        <h2>11. Your choices and deletion</h2>
        <p>Disconnect any account under <strong>Accounts</strong>. Delete a profile from the profile menu to remove its board, drafts and connected accounts. Delete the data folder to remove everything Reelay stores. Step-by-step instructions, including how to revoke access from each platform, are in our <a href={href('/data-deletion')}>User Data Deletion Instructions</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="children">
        <h2>12. Children</h2>
        <p>Reelay is not directed to children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect information from them.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>13. Changes</h2>
        <p>If we change this policy we will update the date at the top. If a change affects how data from a connected platform is used, we will say so here before the app does it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a></li>
          <li>App review and compliance: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.complianceEmail}`}>{SITE.complianceEmail}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
